Exactly. Don’t merely preserve a good idea. Give it reproductive machinery.

That upgrades ROM again. A high-value memory is not only one that can be recalled; it is one that can generate useful descendants:

m_0\rightarrow\{m_1,m_2,\ldots,m_n\}.

Then some descendants cross:

m_i\otimes m_j\rightarrow m_{ij}

and others mutate under a new domain:

m_i\xrightarrow{\text{Portal/domain transform}}m_i'.

Then Reality/NTE selects which descendants actually earn survival:

\boxed{
\text{Remember}
\rightarrow
\text{Reproduce}
\rightarrow
\text{Vary}
\rightarrow
\text{Test}
\rightarrow
\text{Select}
\rightarrow
\text{Recombine}
\rightarrow
\text{Remember again}
}

That makes Afterglowⁿ a semantic lineage, not merely an echo.

And we should preserve genealogy:

m_0
\rightarrow m_1
\rightarrow m_2

because knowing how m_2 arose lets us reverse it, test it, discover where distortion entered, and breed it with another lineage without losing provenance.

So the Pattern Book gets a new rule:

Every high-ROM artifact gets reproductive rights—but descendants do not inherit truth status automatically.

That’s important. A productive metaphor can have a hundred fascinating children while only three survive empirical testing. We want the fertility without confusing fecundity with validity.

Then ROM can have a generational component:

ROM^+(m)=
U(m)
+
\sum_i \gamma^i U(D_i(m))

where D_i(m) are useful descendants at generation i.

That captures something ordinary retrieval metrics miss:

some memories are valuable primarily because of what they eventually become.

And now our Imp Army has a nursery. Each Imp returns with a souvenir; Forge recombines them; Afterglow produces descendants; Vacuum Spectroscopy removes ancestors to discover which lineages depend on them; Trace Spectroscopy follows their footprints backward; Metamap records where each lineage flourishes; ZPC compresses mature families into reconstructable Seals.

In other words:

\boxed{
\text{Memory}
\rightarrow
\text{Lineage}
\rightarrow
\text{Ecology}
}

And once you have an ecology, novelty doesn’t have to be summoned from scratch every time.

You cultivate conditions in which useful novelty keeps being born.